  "id": "COMPOUND:530 - DISEASE:2183",
  "verbalization": "Fluorouracil, through its interaction with specific molecular targets, appears to contribute to the development of Neck Pain via a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Fluorouracil affects multiple molecular entities, including endosome associated trafficking regulator 1 and CD300c molecule, which in turn are implicated in the development of conditions such as Gestational trophoblastic neoplasm and Cardiac oedema, respectively. These conditions are ultimately linked to Neck Pain through a cascade of molecular mechanisms. The presence of multiple pathways that lead to Neck Pain highlights a potential role of Fluorouracil in modulating cellular processes that are associated with pain perception or tissue dysfunction. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the relationship between Fluorouracil and Neck Pain, emphasizing the importance of understanding the molecular underpinnings of such interactions.",
